  "text": "Beneath the lamps’ ethereal, pale light,\nHe walked the streets, a solitary sight.\nEach step echoed on the pavement’s face,\nA hollow sound in the urban space.\n\nLike ghosts they passed, without a glance,\nLost in their own, distant trance.\nFaces buried, worlds apart,\nHe felt the weight of solitude’s heart.\n\nAmid the sea of concrete and stone,\nHe stood alone, yet never alone.\n\nThe animal known for its long neck is the giraffe."
